Toro-Dominguez et al. 2014 shared SLE/RA/SjS signature: inputs of scripts/06b_toro_comparison.R

Source:  Toro-Dominguez D, Carmona-Saez P, Alarcon-Riquelme ME. Shared signatures between
         rheumatoid arthritis, systemic lupus erythematosus and Sjogren's syndrome uncovered
         through gene expression meta-analysis. Arthritis Res Ther 16, 489 (2014).
         doi:10.1186/s13075-014-0489-x (open access, CC BY). Additional file 1,
         13075_2014_489_MOESM1_ESM.xlsx (md5 1d351229342904715db96424f066c573), from
         https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1186%2Fs13075-014-0489-x/MediaObjects/13075_2014_489_MOESM1_ESM.xlsx

Files (the two .csv files are semicolon-separated with decimal commas, exported in April 2026):
  toro2014_signature.csv   sheet "GENE EXPRESSION SIGNATURE": 210 over-expressed and 202
                           under-expressed genes with combined effect size and P value; an
                           asterisk marks the 41 genes not changed in all three diseases, which
                           06b drops, leaving the 371-gene shared signature (188 up, 183 down).
                           SEP15 is kept as text (Excel had turned it into a date).
  toro2014_go_terms.tsv    sheet "GO Analysis": all 115 GO biological-process terms (94 for the
                           over-expressed and 21 for the under-expressed genes) with their gene
                           count, hypergeometric P value and genes, exported on 2026-10-01
                           (tab-separated). 06b uses the 68 terms with P < 0.01 (53 up, 15 down),
                           the terms the original study reports as enriched. Three defects of
                           the sheet are corrected: "KPNB1PSMC2" and "BUB1UBE2C" are split into
                           KPNB1, PSMC2 and BUB1, UBE2C, and "HF17" in GO:0006355 is read as
                           PHF17 (a signature gene; HF17 is not a gene symbol). GO:0000209
                           (protein polyubiquitination) lists 7 genes for a count of 8; it is
                           kept as listed.
  toro2014_gain_genes.csv  sheet "Gain and Loss genes", gain block: the 132 genes found only by
                           the meta-analysis, not in any single dataset.

06b maps every symbol onto the HGNC reference with harmonise_symbols() (scripts/00_config.R)
before comparing it with the atlas genes.
